<title>UK: Bangladesh buys 25,000t white sugar at $338.75/t.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh buys 25,000t white sugar at $338.75/t.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh has bought 25,000 tonnes of June/July white sugar at $338.75 per tonne, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The seller is said to be a Saudi firm.</p>
<p>Traders also said Iraq has bought 12,500 tonnes of Brazilian white sugar at $379 per tonne C&amp;F as part of the oil-for-food programme.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8075</p>
